const step0 = {"summary":"Step 0 of Tahap 6 is finished. The shared contracts, the stub files and the integrator-owned files are in place, so B1, B2 and B3 can start in parallel without touching each other's files. `npx tsc -b` passes. A prod build in .shots/t6-s0/dist measured home JS at 252.7 KB gzip-9 (7 files, under the 253.6 limit). No mini, copy or ecoNav chunk is in the home load, and that dist has been deleted. The control-byte grep printed nothing. Nothing was committed, so the plan's \"tahap6: step 0 contracts\" commit is still yours to make. The `constellation` flag was already in lib/motion.ts.","notDone":["No commit made (task says do not commit; plan step 0.3 'tahap6: step 0 contracts' commit is the integrator's call).","CONTRACTS.md / PERF.md notes not written (integrator, later).","contracts.spec.ts was not run through Playwright: that would start the e2e webServer build. Its logic was checked through tsx instead.","No home-JS baseline from before step 0 was measured, so I can't say whether ECO_SITE in motion.ts (eager) shifted home within ±0.2 KB. Absolute 252.7 KB is under the limit.","No route consumes MINIS or COPIES yet, so the stub minis and copies are not in any built chunk until B1 or B2 import minis.ts."],"handoff":["ALL builders: get minis and copy only through src/demos/minis.ts (MINIS, COPIES, loadMini, loadCopy, useMini, useProductCopy, preloadCopy, preloadMini). Never import a <slug>/copy.ts or <slug>/mini.tsx statically. Do not edit minis.ts, copy-types.ts, ecoNav.check.ts, eco.ts, motion.ts or tests/e2e/tahap6/{helpers,copy.check,contracts}.* (integrator files). Ask the integrator for new eco.ts keys. Timings come from `ECO_SITE` in src/lib/motion.ts, and the `constellation` flag already exists (?off=constellation).","B1 (Ekosistem + Lab): the Lab hover preview is `useMini(slug, hovered)` after `ECO_SITE.mini.previewDelayMs`, keep at most `ECO_SITE.mini.maxMounted`, and render `<C playing={hovered} />`. The test hook is `[data-mini]`, plus `data-mini-step`, which stops changing when paused. For constellation hover or focus call `preloadCopy(slug)`. Constellation timings are `ECO_SITE.constellation` and FlowDiagram uses `ECO_SITE.flow`. Strings: `useEcoI18n().eco.mini.*` and the existing hub/detail/lab keys. Your own files: routes/Ekosistem.tsx, EkosistemDetail.tsx, Lab.tsx, routes/eco/**, content/ecoPages.ts (+ .en.ts), styles/eco-site.css, tests/e2e/tahap6/ekosistem.spec.ts and lab.spec.ts. Test helpers: `import { open, noHScroll, smallTargets, sameOriginLinks, PHONE, WIDTHS } from './helpers'`.","B2 (Produk): replace all 18 src/demos/<slug>/copy.ts with `export const copy: ProductCopy = {...}` (type in src/demos/copy-types.ts) and delete the `stub` line. Check with `npx tsx tests/e2e/tahap6/copy.check.ts --strict`. Write minis for inti, sapa-warga, meja-pimpinan, naskah-pintar, radar-isu, siaga-wilayah, awas-belanja and cek-berkas, built on mini-kit: `const FRAMES: readonly MiniStep[]` must be a module constant; then `const s = useMiniScript(FRAMES, p.playing, { still: p.frame, onCaption: p.onCaption })` and `<MiniFrame slug kind={PRODUCT_BY_SLUG[slug].frame} eco frame={s.id} step={s.step}>`. You may extend mini-kit.tsx and mini-kit.css but must keep the API. For the hero, `useProductCopy(slug)` returns null while loading, so show skeletons then. Mount the mini with `useMini(slug, nearViewport)` (rootMargin from `ECO_SITE.mini.rootMargin`) and play it while visibility ≥ `ECO_SITE.mini.playThreshold`. If `miniCalm()` is true, keep playing=false until the user presses the 'Putar' button (`eco.mini.play` / `playLabel`). Caption: fill(eco.mini.caption, {caption}). Section titles: eco.product.sections.*. Security blocks: eco.product.security.*. Hero label: eco.product.seeInTourAt. When every mini is real, delete src/demos/copy-stub.ts and src/demos/mini-stub.tsx (and the .mk-poster CSS).","B3 (Situs): Navbar, Footer and home read ONLY src/content/ecoNav.ts: ECO_NAV (name, short, to, audience, accent, count, examples), TOUR_NAV, LAB_NAV, SITE_COUNTS, DEMO_COUNT. You own its values, but keep them in sync: tests/e2e/tahap6/contracts.spec.ts (ecoNavDrift) fails on drift. Write minis for toko-autopilot, pajak-beres, juara-jualan, kenal-mitra, pantau-merek, tenderpilot, katalog-lokal, rapor-usaha, indeks-ekonomi and sinyal-pasar, using the same mini-kit pattern as B2 (a stub already exists in each folder). Home JS is now 252.7 KB, which leaves about 0.9 KB of headroom against 253.6."],"budget":"Home JS 252.7 / 253.6 KB gzip-9 (headroom ~0.9 KB for B3's navbar/footer additions; plan allows +0.6)."}
